# ==============================================================================
# Stocks360 webfrontend — environment configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. In production these are set in the hosting
# provider's dashboard (Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables), NOT in a committed
# file: `.env` is gitignored so a deploy's config lives in one place.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING SECRET GOES IN THIS FILE. EVER.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Vite replaces `import.meta.env.VITE_*` with literal strings at build time, so every
# value below is compiled into the JavaScript downloaded by every visitor. Marking a
# variable "Secret"/"Sensitive" in the Vercel dashboard does not change that — it only
# hides it from the dashboard UI. If you would not paste it into a public GitHub issue,
# it does not belong here.
#
# The two things you might expect to find here are deliberately elsewhere:
#
#   * Firebase Web SDK config (apiKey, authDomain, appId, …) is fetched at runtime from
#     the backend's `GET /auth/config`. One source of truth, so it cannot drift from the
#     project the backend actually verifies tokens against. (Those values are public by
#     design anyway — they are protected by Firebase authorized domains and security
#     rules, not by secrecy.)
#
#   * The Firebase Admin service account and the MongoDB URI are real secrets and live
#     only in `backend/.env`. They have no frontend representation at all.
#
# So there is exactly one variable to set:


# Origin of the Stocks360 FastAPI backend. No trailing slash. REQUIRED.
#
# The production build FAILS if this is unset, rather than shipping a bundle that points
# every visitor's browser at 127.0.0.1 — see assertDeployConfig() in vite.config.ts.
#
# Local dev: 127.0.0.1 rather than localhost, because on Windows `localhost` can resolve
# to ::1 while uvicorn is bound to 127.0.0.1, which surfaces as an opaque network error.
# Production: the deployed API, e.g. https://api.stocks360.com
#
# Whichever origin THIS app is served from must be listed in the backend's
# CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS, or every request fails CORS preflight. Locally that is
# http://localhost:5173; in production it is your Vercel domain (and, if you want
# working preview deployments, their domains too).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
